# confirmed/approved and is authoritative for this release. No ORCID or affiliation is set for
# any author: none was supplied to this preparation task and none is invented here.
abstract: >
  Pipeline code, prompt templates, configuration files, schemas, evaluation/audit scripts, and
  documentation for the auditable concept-harmonisation workflow described in the manuscript
  "Auditable Concept Harmonisation for Bibliometric Thematic Analysis: Benchmarking Pairwise
  Equivalence and Downstream Effects". This is the strengthened evidence base prepared following
  an editorial invitation to resubmit: a 900-pair prospective held-out benchmark (400
  circular-economy + 500 diabetes-mellitus pairs, gold-labelled 264 match / 629 non-match / 7
  uncertain) evaluated against eight baselines plus a primary LLM-based method (claude-haiku-4-5)
  and a second-provider robustness check (gpt-5.4-nano), with paired bootstrap comparison,
  selective-prediction/AURC analysis, retrieval-augmented (B8) diagnostics, and a
  transitive-contradiction safety check. Primary method pooled precision/recall/F1 on the
  prospective benchmark: 0.9766 / 0.9579 / 0.9671 at 97.2% coverage. The original (pre-repair)
  500-pair legacy benchmark (351 development + 149 held-out pairs) is preserved as the
  development-phase result, not the primary reported result.
